H1:`Original: אב

Transliteration: 'âb

Phonetic: awb

BDB Definition:

1.  father of an individual
2.  of God as father of his people
3.  head or founder of a household, group, family, or clan
4.  ancestor
    a.  grandfather, forefathers - of person
    b.  of people
5.  originator or patron of a class, profession, or art
6.  of producer, generator (figuratively)
7.  of benevolence and protection (figuratively)
8.  term of respect and honour
9.  ruler or chief (specifically)

Origin: a root

TWOT entry: 4a

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: A primitive word; father in a literal and
immediate, or figurative and remote application: - chief, (fore-) father
([-less]), X patrimony, principal. Compare names in " Abi-"`,
//==========================================================
H2:`Original: אב

Transliteration: 'ab

Phonetic: ab

BDB Definition:

1.  father

Origin: corresponding to H1

TWOT entry: 2553

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: (Chaldee); corresponding to H1: - father.`,
//==========================================================
H3:`Original: אב

Transliteration: 'êb

Phonetic: abe

BDB Definition:

1.  freshness, fresh green, green shoots, or greenery

Origin: from the same as H24

TWOT entry: 1a

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: From the same as H24; a green plant: - greenness,
fruit.`,
//==========================================================
H4:`Original: אב

Transliteration: 'êb

Phonetic: abe

BDB Definition:

1.  fruit, fresh, young, greening

Origin: corresponding to H3

TWOT entry: 2554

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: (Chaldee); corresponding to H3: - fruit.`,
//==========================================================
H5:`Original: אבגתא

Transliteration: 'ăbagthâ'

Phonetic: ab-ag-thaw'

BDB Definition: Abagtha = " God-given"

1.  one of the seven eunuchs in the Persian court of Ahasuerus

Origin: of foreign origin

TWOT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Proper Name Masculine

Strong's Definition: Of foreign origin; Abagtha, a eunuch of Xerxes: -
Abagtha.`,
//==========================================================
H6:`Original: אבד

Transliteration: 'âbad

Phonetic: aw-bad'

BDB Definition:

1.  perish, vanish, go astray, be destroyed
    a.  (Qal)
        1.  perish, die, be exterminated
        2.  perish, vanish (figuratively)
        3.  be lost, strayed
    b.  (Piel)
        1.  to destroy, kill, cause to perish, to give up
        2.  to blot out, do away with, cause to vanish, (figuratively)
        3.  cause to stray, lose
    c.  (Hiphil)
        1.  to destroy, put to death
            a.  of divine judgment
        2.  object name of kings (figuratively)

Origin: a primitive root

TWOT entry: 2

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: A primitive root; properly to wander away, that is
lose oneself; by implication to perish (causatively, destroy): - break,
destroy (-uction), + not escape, fail, lose, (cause to, make) perish,
spend, X and surely, take, be undone, X utterly, be void of, have no way
to flee.`,
//==========================================================
H7:`Original: אבד

Transliteration: 'ăbad

Phonetic: ab-ad'

BDB Definition:

1.  to perish, vanish
    a.  (Peal) shall perish
    b.  (Aphel) destroy
    c.  (Hophal) be destroyed

Origin: corresponding to H6

TWOT entry: 2555

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: (Chaldee); corresponding to H6: - destroy, perish.`,
//==========================================================
