TWOT entry: 68b, 68c

Part(s) of speech: Adverb PrepositionConjunction

Strong's Definition: From H309; properly the hind part; generally used
as an adverb or conjugation, after (in various senses): - after (that,
-ward), again, at, away from, back (from, -side), behind, beside, by,
follow (after, -ing), forasmuch, from, hereafter, hinder end, + out
(over) live, + persecute, posterity, pursuing, remnant, seeing, since,
thence [-forth], when, with.`,
