        1.  to cause to trust, make secure
2.  (TWOT) to feel safe, be careless

Origin: a primitive root

TWOT entry: 233

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: A primitive root; properly to hie for refuge (but
not so precipitately as H2620); figuratively to trust, be confident or
sure: - be bold (confident, secure, sure), careless (one, woman), put
confidence, (make to) hope, (put, make to) trust.`,
