H1197:`Original: בּער

Transliteration: bâ‛ar

Phonetic: baw-ar'

BDB Definition:

1.  to burn, consume, kindle, be kindled (verb)
    a.  (Qal)
        1.  to begin to burn, be kindled, start burning
        2.  to burn, be burning
        3.  to burn, consume
        4.  Jehovah's wrath, human wrath (figuratively)
    b.  (Piel)
        1.  to kindle, burn
        2.  to consume, remove (of guilt) (figuratively)
    c.  (Hiphil)
        1.  to kindle
        2.  to burn up
        3.  to consume (destroy)
    d.  (Pual) to burn
2.  to be stupid, brutish, barbarous (verbal denominative)
    a.  (Qal) to be stupid, dull-hearted, unreceptive
    b.  (Niphal) to be stupid, dull-hearted
    c.  (Piel) to feed, graze
    d.  (Hiphil) to cause to be grazed over

Origin: a primitive root

TWOT entry: 263

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: A primitive root; to kindle, that is, consume (by
fire or by eating); also (as denominative from H1198) to be (become)
brutish: - be brutish, bring (put, take) away, burn, (cause to) eat
(up), feed, heat, kindle, set ([on fire]), waste.`,
