thus to be (clamorously) foolish ; to rave ; causatively to celebrate ;
also to stultify: - (make) boast (self), celebrate, commend, (deal,
make), fool (-ish, -ly), glory, give [light], be (make, feign self) mad
(against), give in marriage, [sing, be worthy of] praise, rage,
renowned, shine.`,
