H2148:`Original: זכריהוּ זכריה

Transliteration: zekaryâh zekaryâhû

Phonetic: zek-ar-yaw'

BDB Definition: Zechariah = " Jehovah remembers"

1.  11th in order of the minor prophets; a priest, son of Berechiah and
    grandson of Iddo, who, along with Haggai, directed the rebuilding of
    the temple in the days of Zerubbabel
2.  king of Israel, son of Jeroboam II
3.  son of Meshelemiah of Shelemiah, a Korhite, and keeper of the north
    gate of the tabernacle of the congregation
4.  one of the sons of Jehiel
5.  a Levite of the second order in the temple band in the time of David
6.  one of the princes of Judah in the reign of Jehoshaphat
7.  son of the high priest Jehoiada, in the reign of Joash king of
    Judah, who was stoned in the court of the temple
8.  a Kohathite Levite in the reign of Josiah
9.  the leader of the sons of Pharosh who returned with Ezra
    a.  son of Bebai
    b.  one of the chiefs of the people whom Ezra summoned in council at
        the river Ahava; stood at Ezra's left hand when Ezra expounded
        the law to the people
    c.  one of the family of Elam who had married a foreign wife after
        the captivity
    d.  ancestor of Athaiah or Uthai
    e.  a Shilonite, descendant of Perez, grandfather of Athaiah
    f.  a priest, son of Pashur
    g.  the representative of the priestly family of Iddo in the days of
        Joiakim the son of Jeshua; possibly the same as 1 above
    h.  one of the priests, son of Jonathan, who blew with the trumpets
        at the dedication of the city wall by Ezra and Nehemiah
    i.  a chief of the Reubenites at the time of the captivity by
        Tiglath-pileser
    j.  one of the priests who accompanied the ark from the house of
        Obed-edom
    k.  son of Isshiah of Jesiah, a Kohathite Levite descended from
        Uzziel
    l.  4th son of Hosah, of the children of Merari
    m.  a Manassite, father of Iddo
    n.  father of Jahaziel. He prophesied in the spirit
    o.  one of the sons of Jehoshaphat
    p.  a prophet in the reign of Uzziah, who appears to have acted as
        the king's counsellor, but of whom nothing is known
    q.  father of Abijah or Abi, Hezekiah's mother
    r.  one of the family of Asaph in the reign of Hezekiah
    s.  one of the rulers of the temple in the reign of Josiah
    t.  son of Jeberechiah who was taken by the prophet Isaiah as one of
        the 'faithful witnesses to record' when he wrote concerning
        Maher-shalal-hash-baz

Origin: from H2142 and H3050

TWOT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Proper Name Masculine

Strong's Definition: From H2142 and H3050; Jah has remembered ;
Zecarjah, the name of twenty nine Israelites: - Zachariah, Zechariah.`,
