        1.  therefore, this being so (specific)
        2.  hitherto
        3.  therefore, on this ground (general)
        4.  afterwards
        5.  in such case
2.  right, just, honest, true, veritable (adjective)
    a.  right, just, honest
    b.  correct
    c.  true, veritable
    d.  true!, right!, correct! (in assent)

Origin: from H3559

TWOT entry: 964a,964b

Part(s) of speech:

Strong's Definition: From H3559; properly set upright; hence
(figuratively as adjective) just ; but usually (as adverb or
conjugation) rightly or so (in various applications to manner, time and
relation; often with other particles): - + after that (this, -ward,
