H4480:`Original: מנּי מנּי מן

Transliteration: min minnı̂y minnêy

Phonetic: min

BDB Definition:

1.  from, out of, on account of, off, on the side of, since, above,
    than, so that not, more than (preposition)
    a.  from (expressing separation), off, on the side of
    b.  out of
        1.  (with verbs of proceeding, removing, expelling)
        2.  (of material from which something is made)
        3.  (of source or origin)
    c.  out of, some of, from (partitively)
    d.  from, since, after (of time)
    e.  than, more than (in comparison)
    f.  from...even to, both...and, either...or
    g.  than, more than, too much for (in comparisons)
    h.  from, on account of, through, because (with infinitive)
2.  that (conjunction)

Origin: from H4482

TWOT entry: 1212,1213e

Part(s) of speech:

Strong's Definition: For H4482; properly a part of; hence
(prepositionally), from or out of in many senses: - above, after, among,
at, because of, by (reason of), from (among), in, X neither, X nor,
(out) of, over, since, X then, through, X whether, with.`,
