H7967:`Original: שׁלּם שׁלּוּם

Transliteration: shallûm shallûm

Phonetic: shal-loom'

BDB Definition: Shallum = " retribution"

1.  son of Jabesh, conspirator and slayer of king Zachariah of the
    northern kingdom of Israel ending the dynasty of Jehu; assumed the
    throne and became the 15th king of the northern kingdom; reigned for
    one month and was killed by Menahem
2.  the 3rd son of king Josiah of Judah and subsequent king of Judah;
    reigned for 3 months before he was taken captive to Egypt where he
    was placed in chains and later died
    a.  also 'Jehoahaz'
3.  husband of Huldah the prophetess in the reign of king Josiah of
    Judah. Maybe the same as 4
4.  uncle of Jeremiah the prophet. Maybe the same as 3
5.  a Simeonite, son of Shaul and grandson of Simeon
6.  a Judaite, son of Sisamai and father of Jekamiah in the family of
    Jerahmeel
7.  an Ephraimite, father of Jehizkiah
8.  a son of Naphtali
9.  a Korahite Levite, chief of a family of gatekeepers for the east
    gate of the temple
    a.  maybe same as 13
    b.  son of Halohesh and ruler of a district of Jerusalem; also
        repairer of the wall of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah
    c.  a priest, of the family of Eleazar, son of Zadok and father of
        Hilkiah in the family line of Ezra
    d.  a Korahite Levite, son of Kore, father of Maaseiah, and in
        charge of the work of the service. Maybe same as 9
    e.  a Levite gatekeeper who had a foreign wife in the time of Ezra
    f.  a Levite and descendant of Bani who had a foreign wife in the
        time of Ezra

Origin: the same as H7966

TWOT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Proper Name Masculine

Strong's Definition: The same as H7966; Shallum, the name of fourteen
Israelites: - Shallum.`,
//==========================================================
