Part(s) of speech:

Strong's Definition: A primitive root; to hear intelligently (often with
implication of attention, obedience, etc.; causatively to tell, etc.): -
X attentively, call (gather) together, X carefully, X certainly,
consent, consider, be content, declare, X diligently, discern, give ear,
(cause to, let, make to) hear (-ken, tell), X indeed, listen, make (a)
noise, (be) obedient, obey, perceive, (make a) proclaim (-ation),
publish, regard, report, shew (forth), (make a) sound, X surely, tell,
understand, whosoever [heareth], witness.`,
