    d.  of a state of separation, that is of distance
        1.  physical, of distance of place
        2.  temporal, of distance of time
2.  of origin
    a.  of the place whence anything is, comes, befalls, is taken
    b.  of origin of a cause

Origin: a primary particle

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech:

Strong's Definition: A primary particle; " off", that is, away (from
something near), in various senses (of place, time, or relation;
literally or figuratively): - (X here-) after, ago, at, because of,
before, by (the space of), for (-th), from, in, (out) of, off, (up-) on
(-ce), since, with. In composition (as a prefix) it usually denotes
separation, departure, cessation, completion, reversal, etc.`,
