G745:`Original: Ἀρχέλαος

Transliteration: Archelaos

Phonetic: ar-khel'-ah-os

Thayer Definition: Archelaus = "prince of the people"

1.  A son of Herod the Great by Malthace, the Samaritan woman. He and
    his brother Antipas were brought up with a certain private man in
    Rome. After the death of his father, he ruled as ethnarch over
    Judaea, Samaria and Idumaea, (with the exception of the cities of
    Gaza, Gadara and Hipo). The Jews and the Samaritans having accused
    him at Rome of tyranny, he was banished by the emperor Augustus to
    Vienna of the Allobroges and died there.

Origin: from G757 and G2994

TDNT entry: None

