G897:`Original: Βαβυλών

Transliteration: Babulōn

Phonetic: bab-oo-lone'

Thayer Definition: Babylon = "confusion"

1.  a very large and famous city, the residence of the Babylonian kings,
    situated on both banks of the Euphrates. Cyrus had formerly captured
    it, but Darius Hystaspis threw down its gates and walls, and Xerxes
    destroyed the temple of Belis. At length the city was reduced to
    almost solitude, the population having been drawn off by the
    neighbouring Seleucia, built on the Tigris by Seleucus Nicanor.
2.  of the territory of Babylonia
3.  allegorically, of Rome as the most corrupt seat of idolatry and the
    enemy of Christianity

Origin: of Hebrew origin H894

TDNT entry: 09:34,9

Part(s) of speech: Noun Location

Strong's Definition: Of Hebrew origin [H894]; Babylon, the capital of
