Phonetic: bar-nab'-as

Thayer Definition: Barnabas = "son of rest"

1.  the surname of Joses or Joseph, a Levite, a native of Cyprus He was
    a distinguished Christian teacher and companion and colleague of
    Paul.

Origin: of Aramaic origin H1247 and H5029

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: Of Chaldee origin [H1247] and [H5029]; son of Nabas
(that is, prophecy); Barnabas, an Israelite: - Barnabas.`,
//==========================================================
G922:`Original: βάρος

Transliteration: baros

Phonetic: bar'-os

Thayer Definition:

