G945:`Original: βαττολογέω

Transliteration: battologeō

Phonetic: bat-tol-og-eh'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to stammer
2.  to repeat the same things over and over, to use many idle words, to
    babble, prate. Some suppose the word derived from Battus, a king of
    Cyrene, who is said to have stuttered; others from Battus, an author
    of tedious and wordy poems.

Origin: from Battos (a proverbial stammerer) and G3056

TDNT entry: 10:57,1

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From Βάττος Battos (a proverbial stammerer) and
G3056; to stutter, that is, (by implication) to prate tediously: - use
vain repetitions.`,
//==========================================================
