//==========================================================
G1611:`Original: ἔκστασις

Transliteration: ekstasis

Phonetic: ek'-stas-is

Thayer Definition:

1.  any casting down of a thing from its proper place or state,
    displacement
2.  a throwing of the mind out of its normal state, alienation of mind,
    whether such as makes a lunatic or that of a man who by some sudden
    emotion is transported as it were out of himself, so that in this
    rapt condition, although he is awake, his mind is drawn off from all
    surrounding objects and wholly fixed on things divine that he sees
    nothing but the forms and images lying within, and thinks that he
    perceives with his bodily eyes and ears realities shown him by God.
3.  amazement, the state of one who, either owing to the importance or
    the novelty of an event, is thrown into a state of blended fear and
    wonderment

Origin: from G1839

TDNT entry: 09:29,2

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: From G1839; a displacement of the mind, that is,
bewilderment, " ecstasy" : - + be amazed, amazement, astonishment,
trance.`,
//==========================================================
