        1.  in a good sense, to be zealous in the pursuit of good
    b.  to desire earnestly, pursue
        1.  to desire one earnestly, to strive after, busy one's self
            about him
        2.  to exert one's self for one (that he may not be torn from
            me)
        3.  to be the object of the zeal of others, to be zealously
            sought after
    c.  to envy

Origin: from G2205

TDNT entry: 16:42,3

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2205; to have warmth of feeling for or
against: - affect, covet (earnestly), (have) desire, (move with) envy,
