//==========================================================
G2222:`Original: ζωή

Transliteration: zōē

Phonetic: dzo-ay'

Thayer Definition:

1.  life
    a.  the state of one who is possessed of vitality or is animate
    b.  every living soul
2.  life
    a.  of the absolute fulness of life, both essential and ethical,
        which belongs to God, and through him both to the hypostatic
        "logos" and to Christ in whom the "logos" put on human nature
    b.  life real and genuine, a life active and vigorous, devoted to
