        Holies, which was sprinkled with the blood of the expiatory
        victim on the annual day of atonement (this rite signifying that
        the life of the people, the loss of which they had merited by
        their sins, was offered to God in the blood as the life of the
        victim, and that God by this ceremony was appeased and their
        sins expiated); hence the lid of expiation, the propitiatory
    b.  an expiatory sacrifice
    c.  a expiatory victim

Origin: from a derivative of G2433

TDNT entry: 08:18,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Neuter

Strong's Definition: Neuter of a derivative of G2433; an expiatory
