        1.  utensils, food
        2.  a leper, to cleanse by curing
        3.  to remove by cleansing
    b.  in a moral sense
        1.  to free from defilement of sin and from faults
        2.  to purify from wickedness
        3.  to free from guilt of sin, to purify
        4.  to consecrate by cleansing or purifying
        5.  to consecrate, dedicate
2.  to pronounce clean in a levitical sense

Origin: from G2513

TDNT entry: 09:53,4

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2513; to cleanse (literally or
figuratively): - (make) clean (-se), purge, purify.`,
//==========================================================
G2512:`Original: καθαρισμός

Transliteration: katharismos

Phonetic: kath-ar-is-mos'

Thayer Definition:

1.  a cleansing, purification, a ritual purgation or washing
