    b.  of levitical purification of women after childbirth
    c.  a cleansing from the guilt of sins wrought by the expiatory
        sacrifice of Christ

Origin: from G2511

TDNT entry: 10:09,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: From G2511; a washing off, that is, (ceremonially)
ablution, (morally) expiation: - cleansing, + purge, purification,
(-fying).`,
