G2664:`Original: καταπαύω

Transliteration: katapauō

Phonetic: kat-ap-ow'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to make quiet, to cause to be at rest, to grant rest
    a.  to lead to a quiet abode
    b.  to still, restrain, to cause (one striving to do something) to
        desist
2.  to rest, take rest

Origin: from G2596 and G3973

TDNT entry: 13:27,4

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G3973; to settle down, that is,
(literally) to colonize, or (figuratively) to (cause to) desist: -
cease, (give) rest (-rain).`,
//==========================================================
G2665:`Original: καταπέτασμα

Transliteration: katapetasma

Phonetic: kat-ap-et'-as-mah

Thayer Definition:

1.  a veil spread out, a curtain
    a.  the name given to the two curtains in the temple at Jerusalem,
        one of them at the entrance to the temple separated the Holy
        Place from the outer court, the other veiled the Holy of Holies
        from the Holy Place

Origin: from a compound of G2596 and a congener of G4072

TDNT entry: 13:28,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Neuter

Strong's Definition: From a compound of G2596 and a congener of G4072;
something spread thoroughly, that is, (specifically) the door screen (to
the Most Holy Place) in the Jewish Temple: - vail.`,
//==========================================================
G2666:`Original: καταπίνω

Transliteration: katapinō

Phonetic: kat-ap-ee'-no

