G2718:`Original: κατέρχομαι

Transliteration: katerchomai

Phonetic: kat-er'-khom-ahee

Thayer Definition:

1.  to come down, go down
    a.  of one who goes from a higher to a lower locality
    b.  of those who come to a place by a ship

Origin: from G2596 and G2064 (including its alternate)

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G2064 (including its alternate); to
come (or go) down (literally or figuratively): - come (down), depart,
descend, go down, land.`,
//==========================================================
G2719:`Original: κατεσθίω

Transliteration: katesthiō

Phonetic: kat-es-thee'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to consume by eating, to eat up, devour
    a.  of birds
    b.  of a dragon
    c.  of a man eating up the little book
2.  metaphorically
    a.  to devour, i.e. squander, waste: substance
    b.  to devour, i.e. forcibly appropriate: widows' property
    c.  to strip one of his goods
        1.  to ruin (by the infliction of injuries)
    d.  by fire, to devour, i.e. to utterly consume, destroy
    e.  of the consumption of the strength of body and mind by strong
        emotions

Origin: from G2596 and G2068 (including its alternate)

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G2068 (including its alternate); to
eat down, that is, devour (literally or figuratively): - devour.`,
//==========================================================
G2720:`Original: κατευθύνω

Transliteration: kateuthunō

Phonetic: kat-yoo-thoo'-no

Thayer Definition:

1.  to make straight, guide, direct
    a.  of the removal of the hindrances to coming to one

Origin: from G2596 and G2116

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2590 and G2116; to straighten fully, that is,
(figuratively) direct: - guide, direct.`,
//==========================================================
G2721:`Original: κατεφίστημι

Transliteration: katephistēmi

Phonetic: kat-ef-is'-tay-mee

Thayer Definition:

1.  to set up against

Origin: from G2596 and G2186

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G2186; to stand over against, that
is, rush upon (assault): - make insurrection against.`,
//==========================================================
G2722:`Original: κατέχω

Transliteration: katechō

Phonetic: kat-ekh'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to hold back, detain, retain
    a.  from going away
    b.  to restrain, hinder (the course or progress of)
        1.  that which hinders, Antichrist from making his appearance
        2.  to check a ship's headway, i.e. to hold or head the ship
    c.  to hold fast, keep secure, keep firm possession of
2.  to get possession of, take
    a.  to possess

Origin: from G2596 and G2192

TDNT entry: 15:49,3

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G2192; to hold down (fast), in
various applications (literally or figuratively): - have, hold (fast),
keep (in memory), let, X make toward, possess, retain, seize on, stay,
take, withhold.`,
//==========================================================
G2723:`Original: κατηγορέω

Transliteration: katēgoreō

Phonetic: kat-ay-gor-eh'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to accuse
    a.  before a judge: to make an accusation
    b.  of an extra-judicial accusation

Origin: from G2725

TDNT entry: 13:37,4

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2725; to be a plaintiff, that is, to charge
with some offence: - accuse, object.`,
//==========================================================
G2724:`Original: κατηγορία

Transliteration: katēgoria

Phonetic: kat-ay-gor-ee'-ah

Thayer Definition:

1.  accusation, charge

Origin: from G2725

TDNT entry: 13:37,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: From G2725; a complaint (" category" ), that is,
criminal charge: - accusation (X -ed).`,
//==========================================================
G2725:`Original: κατήγορος

Transliteration: katēgoros

Phonetic: kat-ay'-gor-os

Thayer Definition:

1.  an accuser
    a.  a name given to the devil by the rabbis

Origin: from G2596 and G58

TDNT entry: 13:36,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G58; against one in the assembly,
that is, a complainant at law; specifically Satan: - accuser.`,
//==========================================================
G2726:`Original: κατήφεια

Transliteration: katēpheia

Phonetic: kat-ay'-fi-ah

Thayer Definition:

1.  a downcast look expressive of sorrow
2.  shame, dejection, gloom

Origin: from a compound of G2596 and perhaps a derivative of the base of
G5316 (meaning downcast in look)

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: From a compound of G2596 and perhaps a derivative
of the base of G5316 (meaning downcast in look); demureness, that is,
(by implication) sadness: - heaviness.`,
//==========================================================
G2727:`Original: κατηχέω

Transliteration: katēcheō

Phonetic: kat-ay-kheh'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to sound towards, sound down upon, resound
    a.  to charm with resounding sound, to fascinate
2.  to teach orally, to instruct
3.  to inform by word of mouth
    a.  to be orally informed

Origin: from G2596 and G2279

TDNT entry: 13:38,4

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G2279; to sound down into the ears,
that is, (by implication) to indoctrinate (" catechize" ) or (generally)
to apprise of: - inform, instruct, teach.`,
//==========================================================
G2728:`Original: κατιόω

Transliteration: katioō

Phonetic: kat-ee-o'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to rust over, cover with rust

Origin: from G2596 and a derivative of G2447

TDNT entry: 3:334,*

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and a derivative of G2447; to rust down,
that is, corrode: - canker.`,
//==========================================================
G2729:`Original: κατισχύω

Transliteration: katischuō

Phonetic: kat-is-khoo'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to be strong to another's detriment, to prevail against
2.  to be superior in strength
3.  to overcome
4.  to prevail

Origin: from G2596 and G2480

TDNT entry: 09:37,4

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G2480; to overpower: - prevail
(against).`,
//==========================================================
G2730:`Original: κατοικέω

Transliteration: katoikeō

Phonetic: kat-oy-keh'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to dwell, settle
    a.  metaphorically divine powers, influences, etc., are said to
        dwell in his soul, to pervade, prompt, govern it
2.  to dwell in, inhabit
    a.  God is said to dwell in the temple, i.e. to be always present
        for worshippers

Origin: from G2596 and G3611

TDNT entry: 07:33,7

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G2596 and G3611; to house permanently, that
is, reside (literally or figuratively): - dwell (-er), inhabitant
(-ter).`,
//==========================================================
G2731:`Original: κατοίκησις

Transliteration: katoikēsis

Phonetic: kat-oy'-kay-sis

Thayer Definition:

1.  dwelling, abode

Origin: from G2730

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: From G2730; residence (properly the act; but by
implication concretely the mansion): - dwelling.`,
//==========================================================
G2732:`Original: κατοικητήριον

Transliteration: katoikētērion

Phonetic: kat-oy-kay-tay'-ree-on

Thayer Definition:

1.  an abode, a habitation

Origin: from a derivative of G2730

TDNT entry: 07:35,7

Part(s) of speech: Noun Neuter

Strong's Definition: From a derivative of G2730; a dwelling place: -
habitation.`,
//==========================================================
G2733:`Original: κατοικία

Transliteration: katoikia

Phonetic: kat-oy-kee'-ah

Thayer Definition:

1.  dwelling, habitation
2.  to cause to dwell, to send or bring into an abode
3.  to give a dwelling to

Origin: a primitive root

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: residence (properly the condition; but by
implication the abode itself): - habitation.`,
//==========================================================
G2734:`Original: κατοπτρίζομαι

Transliteration: katoptrizomai

Phonetic: kat-op-trid'-zom-ahee

Thayer Definition:

1.  to show in a mirror, to make to reflect, to mirror
2.  to look at one's self in a mirror
3.  to behold one's self in a mirror

Origin: middle voice from a compound of G2596 and a derivative of G3700
[cf G2072]

TDNT entry: 13:36,3

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: Middle voice from a compound of G2596 and a
derivative of G3700 (compare G2072); to mirror oneself, that is, to see
reflected (figuratively): - behold as in a glass.`,
//==========================================================
G2735:`Original: κατόρθωμα

Transliteration: katorthōma

Phonetic: kat-or'-tho-mah

Thayer Definition:

1.  a right action, a successful achievement
