Transliteration: kauma

Phonetic: kow'-mah

Thayer Definition:

1.  heat
    a.  of painful and burning heat

Origin: from G2545

TDNT entry: 13:42,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Neuter

Strong's Definition: From G2545; properly a burn (concretely), but used
(abstractly) of a glow: - heat.`,
