3.  in a medical sense, to cauterise, remover by cautery

Origin: from a derivative of G2545

TDNT entry: 3:644,*

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From a derivative of G2545; to brand (" cauterize"
), that is, (by implication) to render unsensitive (figuratively): -
