G2776:`Original: κεφαλή

Transliteration: kephalē

Phonetic: kef-al-ay'

Thayer Definition:

1.  the head, both of men and often of animals. Since the loss of the
    head destroys life, this word is used in the phrases relating to
    capital and extreme punishment.
2.  metaphorically anything supreme, chief, prominent
    a.  of persons, master lord: of a husband in relation to his wife
    b.  of Christ: the Lord of the husband and of the Church
    c.  of things: the corner stone

Origin: from the primary kapto (in the sense of seizing)

TDNT entry: 14:13,4

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: Probably from the primary wordκάπτω kaptō (in the
