G2889:`Original: κόσμος

Transliteration: kosmos

Phonetic: kos'-mos

Thayer Definition:

1.  an apt and harmonious arrangement or constitution, order, government
2.  ornament, decoration, adornment, i.e. the arrangement of the stars,
    'the heavenly hosts', as the ornament of the heavens. 1Pe 3:3
3.  the world, the universe
4.  the circle of the earth, the earth
5.  the inhabitants of the earth, men, the human family
6.  the ungodly multitude; the whole mass of men alienated from God, and
    therefore hostile to the cause of Christ
7.  world affairs, the aggregate of things earthly
    a.  the whole circle of earthly goods, endowments riches,
        advantages, pleasures, etc, which although hollow and frail and
        fleeting, stir desire, seduce from God and are obstacles to the
        cause of Christ
8.  any aggregate or general collection of particulars of any sort
    a.  the Gentiles as contrasted to the Jews (Rom 11:12 etc)
    b.  of believers only, Joh 1:29; Joh 3:16; Joh 3:17; Joh 6:33; Joh
        12:47 1Co 4:9; 2Co 5:19

Origin: probably from the base of G2865

TDNT entry: 17:28,5

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: Probably from the base of G2865; orderly
arrangement, that is, decoration ; by implication the world (in a wide
or narrow sense, including its inhabitants, literally or figuratively
[morally]): - adorning, world.`,
