        1.  especially concerning justice and injustice, right or wrong
    b.  sentence of condemnation, damnatory judgment, condemnation and
        punishment
4.  the college of judges (a tribunal of seven men in the several cities
    of Palestine; as distinguished from the Sanhedrin, which had its
    seat at Jerusalem)
5.  right, justice

Origin: perhaps a primitive word

TDNT entry: 18:41,5

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: (Subjectively or objectively, for or against); by
