G2958:`Original: Κυρήνιος

Transliteration: Kurēnios

Phonetic: koo-ray'-nee-os

Thayer Definition: Cyrenius = "warrior"

1.  the Greek form of the Roman name Quirinus. His full name is Publius
    Sulpicius Quirinus. He was consul B.C. 12., and was made governor of
    Syria after the banishment of Archelaus in A.D. 6. He was probably
    twice governor of Syria; his first governorship extended from B.C. 4
    (the year of Christ's birth) to B.C. 1. It was during this time that
    he was sent to make enrolment which caused Joseph and Mary to visit
    Bethlehem. Luk 2:2. The second enrolment is mentioned in Act 5:37.

Origin: of Latin origin

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: Of Latin origin; Cyrenius (that is, Quirinus), a
Roman: - Cyrenius.`,
