TDNT entry: 09:12,5

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: Middle voice from a probable derivative of G3089
(meaning filth); properly to soil, that is, (figuratively) insult
(maltreat): - make havock of.`,
//==========================================================
G3076:`Original: λυπέω

Transliteration: lupeō

Phonetic: loo-peh'-o

Thayer Definition:

1.  to make sorrowful
2.  to affect with sadness, cause grief, to throw into sorrow
