4.  to make one uneasy, cause him a scruple

Origin: from G3077

TDNT entry: 09:13,5

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G3077; to distress ; reflexively or passively
to be sad: - cause grief, grieve, be in heaviness, (be) sorrow (-ful),
be (make) sorry.`,
//==========================================================
G3077:`Original: λύπη

Transliteration: lupē

Phonetic: loo'-pay

