        and others, to the wise men, teachers, priests, physicians,
        astrologers, seers, interpreters of dreams, augers, soothsayers,
        sorcerers etc.
    b.  the oriental wise men (astrologers) who, having discovered by
        the rising of a remarkable star that the Messiah had just been
        born, came to Jerusalem to worship him
    c.  a false prophet and sorcerer

Origin: of foreign origin H7248

TDNT entry: 09:56,5

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: Of foreign origin [H7248]; a Magian, that is,
Oriental scientist ; by implication a magician: - sorcerer, wise man.`,
