Origin: of Hebrew origin H4478

TDNT entry: 11:42,6

Part(s) of speech: Noun Neuter

Strong's Definition: Of Hebrew origin [H4478]; manna (that is, man), an
edible gum: - manna.`,
//==========================================================
G3132:`Original: μαντεύομαι

Transliteration: manteuomai

Phonetic: mant-yoo'-om-ahee

Thayer Definition:

1.  to act as a seer
    a.  deliver an oracle, prophesy, divine

Origin: from a derivative of G3105 (meaning a prophet, as supposed to
rave through inspiration)

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From a derivative of G3105 (meaning a prophet, as
supposed to rave through inspiration); to divine, that is, utter spells
(under pretence of foretelling): - by soothsaying.`,
//==========================================================
G3133:`Original: μαραίνω

Transliteration: marainō

Phonetic: mar-ah'-ee-no

Thayer Definition:

1.  to extinguish (a flame, fire, light, etc.)
