2.  to conjure, beseech as in God's name, exhort solemnly

Origin: middle voice from G3144

TDNT entry: 12:30,6

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: Middle voice from G3144; to be adduced as a
witness, that is, (figuratively) to obtest (in affirmation or
exhortation): - take to record, testify.`,
//==========================================================
G3144:`Original: μάρτυς

Transliteration: martus

Phonetic: mar'-toos

Thayer Definition:

1.  a witness
    a.  in a legal sense
    b.  an historical sense
        1.  one who is a spectator of anything, e.g. of a contest
    c.  in an ethical sense
        1.  those who after his example have proved the strength and
            genuineness of their faith in Christ by undergoing a violent
            death

Origin: of uncertain affinity

TDNT entry: 11:54,6

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: Of uncertain affinity; a witness (literally
[judicially] or figuratively [generally]); by analogy a " martyr" : -
martyr, record, witness.`,
//==========================================================
