//==========================================================
G3844:`Original: παρά

Transliteration: para

Phonetic: par-ah'

Thayer Definition:

1.  from, of at, by, besides, near

Origin: a root word

TDNT entry: 17:07,8

Part(s) of speech: Preposition

Strong's Definition: A primary preposition; properly near, that is,
(with genitive case) from beside (literally or figuratively), (with
dative case) at (or in) the vicinity of (objectively or subjectively),
(with accusative case) to the proximity with (local [especially beyond
or opposed to] or causal [on account of]). In compounds it retains the
same variety of application: - above, against, among, at, before, by,
contrary to, X friend, from, + give [such things as they], + that [she]
had, X his, in, more than, nigh unto, (out) of, past, save, side. .. by,
in the sight of, than, [there-] fore, with. In compounds it retains the
same variety of application.`,
//==========================================================
G3845:`Original: παραβαίνω

Transliteration: parabainō

