//==========================================================
G3856:`Original: παραδειγματίζω

Transliteration: paradeigmatizō

Phonetic: par-ad-igue-mat-id'-zo

Thayer Definition:

1.  to set forth as a public example, make an example of
    a.  in a bad sense
        1.  to hold up to infamy
        2.  to expose to public disgrace

Origin: from G3844 and G1165

TDNT entry: 02:32,1

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: From G3844 and G1165; to show alongside (the
