5.  persuasive discourse, stirring address
    a.  instructive, admonitory, conciliatory, powerful hortatory
        discourse

Origin: from G3870

TDNT entry: 17:53,8

Part(s) of speech: Noun Feminine

Strong's Definition: From G3870; imploration, hortation, solace: -
comfort, consolation, exhortation, intreaty.`,
//==========================================================
G3875:`Original: παράκλητος

Transliteration: paraklētos

Phonetic: par-ak'-lay-tos

Thayer Definition:

1.  summoned, called to one's side, especially called to one's aid
    a.  one who pleads another's cause before a judge, a pleader,
        counsel for defense, legal assistant, an advocate
    b.  one who pleads another's cause with one, an intercessor
        1.  of Christ in his exaltation at God's right hand, pleading
            with God the Father for the pardon of our sins
    c.  in the widest sense, a helper, succourer, aider, assistant
        1.  of the Holy Spirit destined to take the place of Christ with
            the apostles (after his ascension to the Father), to lead
            them to a deeper knowledge of the gospel truth, and give
            them divine strength needed to enable them to undergo trials
            and persecutions on behalf of the divine kingdom

Origin: a root word

TDNT entry: 18:20,8

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: An intercessor, consoler: - advocate, comforter.`,
//==========================================================
G3876:`Original: παρακοή

