2.  to wring one's neck, throttle

Origin: strengthened from G4154

TDNT entry: 13:35,9

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: Strengthened from G4154; to wheeze, that is,
(causative by implication) to throttle or strangle (drown): - choke,
take by the throat.`,
//==========================================================
G4156:`Original: πνικτός

Transliteration: pniktos

Phonetic: pnik-tos'

Thayer Definition:

1.  suffocate, strangled
    a.  what is strangled, i.e. an animal deprived of life without the
