    deemed the written law alone to be obligatory on the nation, as the
    divine authority. They denied the following doctrines:
    a.  resurrection of the body
    b.  immortality of the soul
    c.  existence of spirits and angels
    d.  divine predestination, affirmed free will

Origin: probably from G4524

TDNT entry: 07:36,0

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

