G4566:`Original: Σατᾶν

Transliteration: Satan

Phonetic: sat-an'

Thayer Definition:

1.  adversary (one who opposes another in purpose or act), the name
    given to
    a.  the prince of evil spirits, the inveterate adversary of God and
        Christ
        1.  he incites apostasy from God and to sin
        2.  circumventing men by his wiles
        3.  the worshippers of idols are said to be under his control
        4.  by his demons he is able to take possession of men and
            inflict them with diseases
        5.  by God's assistance he is overcome
        6.  on Christ's return from heaven he will be bound with chains
            for a thousand years, but when the thousand years are
            finished he will walk the earth in yet greater power, but
            shortly after will be given over to eternal punishment
    b.  a Satan-like man

Origin: of Hebrew origin H7854

TDNT entry: 7:151,*

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: Of Hebrew origin [H7854]; Satan, that is, the
devil: - Satan. Compare G4567.`,
