        gospel
    d.  one who with others acknowledges the same Lord, Jesus, and obeys
        his commands
    e.  one who with others is subject to the same divine authority in
        the Messianic economy
        1.  of angels as the fellow servants of Christians

Origin: from G4862 and G1401

TDNT entry: 06:21,2

Part(s) of speech: Noun Masculine

Strong's Definition: From G4862 and G1401; a co-slave, that is, servitor
or ministrant of the same master (human or divine): - fellowservant.`,
