        2.  to preserve one who is in danger of destruction, to save or
            rescue
    b.  to save in the technical biblical sense
        1.  negatively
            a.  to deliver from the penalties of the Messianic judgment
            b.  to save from the evils which obstruct the reception of
                the Messianic deliverance

