//==========================================================
G5175:`Original: Τρωγύλλιον

Transliteration: Trōgullion

Phonetic: tro-gool'-lee-on

Thayer Definition: Trogyllium = "a cache"

1.  the name of a town and a promontory of Ionia, not far from the
    island of Samos, at the foot of Mt. Mycale between Ephesus and the
    mouth of the river Maeander

Origin: of uncertain derivation

TDNT entry: None

Part(s) of speech: Noun Location

Strong's Definition: Of uncertain derivation; Trogyllium, a place in
