//==========================================================
G5271:`Original: ὑποκρίνομαι

Transliteration: hupokrinomai

Phonetic: hoop-ok-rin'-om-ahee

Thayer Definition:

1.  to take up another's statements in reference to what one has decided
    for one's self
    a.  to reply, answer
2.  to make answer (speak) on the stage
    a.  to impersonate anyone, play a part
3.  to simulate, feign, pretend

Origin: middle voice from G5259 and G2919

TDNT entry: 17:19,1

Part(s) of speech: Verb

Strong's Definition: Middle voice from G5259 and G2919; to decide (speak
