Strong's Definition: Probably strengthened from φθίω phthiō (to pine or
waste): properly to shrivel or wither, that is, to spoil (by any
process) or (genitive) to ruin (especially figuratively by moral
influences, to deprave): - corrupt (self), defile, destroy.`,
